cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NeuroRule in research, please cite the software using this metadata."
title: "NeuroRule: interpretable analysis of small datasets with neurofuzzy networks"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "B. Iglesias Otero"
repository-code: "https://github.com/BraisIglesias17/NeuroRules"
url: "https://github.com/BraisIglesias17/NeuroRules"
abstract: >-
  NeuroRule is a desktop data-analysis application for small datasets. It
  combines preprocessing, exploratory statistics, conventional machine-learning
  models, and an interpretable zero-order Sugeno neurofuzzy regressor whose
  antecedents can be inspected as linguistic rules.
keywords:
  - neurofuzzy systems
  - interpretable machine learning
  - small datasets
  - data analysis
  - Sugeno inference
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
